The '''Kwangju national football team''' ({{Lang-ko|광주 축구 국가대표팀}}) represents the [[Kwangju]] autonomous region of [[Daras]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Kwangju Football Association]] and competes as a member of the Central Fosian Football Federation within the [[AFA]] confederation.

Kwangju are currently ranked 33rd in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and qualified for their second [[AFA World Cup]] at the [[2022 AFA World Cup|2022 tournament]].

== History ==

=== Autonomous football ===
Kwangju's separate football identity dates from the 1990 agreement that allowed the autonomous region to field its own national team in AFA competitions, similar to other sub-national football associations in the Adonian system. The Kwangju K-League, founded in 1993, has produced technically skilled players who have moved to clubs across Daras and the wider Fosian region.

=== World Cup appearances ===
Kwangju first qualified for the World Cup in 2010, exiting at the group stage but earning a notable draw. The 2022 qualification marks only their second appearance, with a squad featuring a strong domestic core and several diaspora players from Darasian and East Fosian clubs.

